This repository is public to be read, not to be reused as is. It contains two things, under two regimes.


1. THE IDENTITY — ALL RIGHTS RESERVED

Florian Etourneau's visual identity is protected by copyright. It includes:

- the starling, in all its poses and variants (logo, head, perched, flying, cocked to shoot, articulated
  into parts), and the family on the wire;
- the images in logo/, illustrations/, avatars/, favicon/ and profile/, and the icons in icons/ (the SVGs
  and the sprite);
- the brand guidelines (charte/);
- the texts (README.md);
- the name "Florian Etourneau" used as a signature, and the whole formed by the palette, the typefaces
  and the motifs (the point, the wire, the murmuration);
- the identity's paths, shapes and values contained in the code: the starling's silhouettes and parts,
  the shapes drawn by the murmuration, the token values (tokens/tokens.json and tokens.css).

You may view them here. Any reproduction, modification, adaptation or distribution, in whole or in part,
requires the author's written consent: florian.etourneau@gmail.com.


2. THE CODE — MIT LICENSE

The code in this repository is under the MIT license: the scripts (scripts/), the starling (starling/*.js)
and the murmuration (murmuration/*.js), and the code of the demo pages.

The license covers the code, not what it draws: the identity's paths and values it contains remain
subject to part 1. To reuse the code, replace them with your own.

